WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.760
- Now I could not be more excited
than I am for today's show

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.760
because it has a theme, a
very strong theme actually.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:12.380
It's literally been 22
years in the making.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:16.420
Back in 1999 I was
lucky enough to be in it

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.980
and it's just really near
and dear to my heart.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:20.922
It's 'Never Been Kissed'.

00:00:20.922 --> 00:00:24.755
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.130
And today I am actually
reuniting with some of the cast.

00:00:36.043 --> 00:00:38.900
(crowd cheering and clapping)

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:43.470
Because also, who doesn't love a reunion,

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.440
but first in honor of 'Never Been Kissed',

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.130
we have a viewer who wrote

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:53.130
in 'Looking for Help in the
Love Department' and Tasha says

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.400
that she has never been
kissed by her new boyfriend.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:02.590
So she's gonna join us now

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.250
from the California State baseball field.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:09.300
Tasha, hello.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.630
- Hey Drew.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.910
So yes, my boyfriend Hunter and I,

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:16.292
we started dating over the
summer during the pandemic

00:01:16.292 --> 00:01:20.060
and we actually met five years ago

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.310
and essentially we were
dating other people

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.920
so we just became really
good friends over the years

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.810
and about three months ago,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.110
we decided to take our
relationship to the next level

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.033
and now we are official.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:38.380
So now it's just a matter of
us having this first kiss,

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.850
which we have not had yet.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.930
- [Drew] Well, let me just
ask a question that comes

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:43.763
to my mind.

00:01:43.763 --> 00:01:46.030
Why has there been no kiss so far?

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.410
(crowd laughs)

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:51.570
- Honestly, I feel like we
just have the classic case

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:54.370
of Ross and Rachel Syndrome,
where we've been friends

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:57.940
for so long and now there's
just this big buildup

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.550
and we're both so nervous and excited

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.210
and we want it to be perfect.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:08.070
And I sent Hunter a text this
morning, inviting him here.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:11.160
And I said, you know, 'I
don't want a response.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.510
Just trust me and show up if
you are ready to take this

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.850
to the next level and
make it the real deal.'

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:22.280
So I'm here at the pitcher's
mound at Cal State.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.380
I have no idea if he's
gonna show up or not,

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.370
but you only live once, right?

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:30.787
(crowd cheers and claps)

00:02:34.406 --> 00:02:35.320
- I love this.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.710
This moment is special
and we're all invested

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:38.700
in it with you.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.670
We're gonna check in with you

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:44.810
and let's see if we can create
a happy ending for today.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.370
(crowd clapping and cheering)

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.590
At the beginning of the show,

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:51.080
we met Tasha who has asked for help

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.180
in the romance department
three months ago.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.590
Tasha's best friend,
Hunter became her boyfriend

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.000
and yet she's never been kissed by him.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.620
How perfect is that for our
'Never Been Kissed' reunion.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.290
Now, Tasha has asked Hunter to meet her

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:13.830
on the pitcher's mound at
California State University

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.420
if he's ready to make this thing real.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.820
Here's hoping.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:22.004
Let's check in and see if he's arrived.

00:03:22.004 --> 00:03:26.250
(crowd clapping and cheering)

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.300
I'm nervous, I'm so invested in this.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.090
Tasha, how are you feeling?

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.243
- Pretty nervous, lots of butterflies.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.880
I have no idea if he's gonna show up,

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.840
I have a feeling he will.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:45.040
- Um, this is a fantasy
and yet it's your reality

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:48.770
and we're here to support you and uh wait,

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:50.083
I'm just getting word.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.684
Hunter is there.

00:03:52.684 --> 00:03:54.281
(crowd claps and cheers)

00:03:54.281 --> 00:03:56.948
( music starts)

00:04:02.445 --> 00:04:07.445
(crowd claps and cheers,
music plays in background)

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:28.673
Hi guys.

00:04:28.673 --> 00:04:31.220
- We were in the middle of something.

00:04:33.707 --> 00:04:36.443
- I'm so happy for you both.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.254
You know, there's um-

00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:41.000
- Thank you for making this happen.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.770
- There's an old saying that

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:45.793
some of the best relationships
come out of friendship.

00:04:47.103 --> 00:04:50.703
(crowd claps and cheers)

00:04:50.703 --> 00:04:54.720
(Tasha speaks inaudibly)

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.103
Hunter, how you feel?

00:04:58.630 --> 00:04:59.682
- Pretty good.

00:04:59.682 --> 00:05:01.400
(crowd laughs)

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.693
It was a long time coming, yeah.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:08.683
- And Tasha, how do you feel?

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.063
- Very happy, very thankful.

00:05:14.451 --> 00:05:17.070
(crowd clapping and cheering)

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.690
- Congratulations on showing

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:22.640
that fantasies can become reality

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:26.940
and thank you for letting us
all be a part of this moment.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:29.270
We wish you the very best.

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.000
Thanks for watching everyone.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.491
Join us tomorrow for
another sunny day in LA

00:05:36.491 --> 00:05:38.473
as we bid you good night.

00:05:38.473 --> 00:05:40.579
(crowd clapping and cheering)

00:05:40.579 --> 00:05:43.162
(upbeat music)

